    pr_ref:  # 8c0d
    description: "Five tests in tests/test_session_start_agent_notes.py fail inside a fresh CI container but PASS natively in the sandbox -> they are not hermetic. In a clean checkout, when the tests' intended inputs are not fully controlled, the session-start hook takes the \"Autonomous mode is OFF...\" branch instead of emitting the agent_notes-staleness prompt the tests assert on:\n\n  AssertionError: assert 'agent_notes.json was last updated' in 'Autonomous mode is OFF. Before starting work, ask the user which mode to use: BROAD, DEEP, or OFF. Then run: ./scripts/loop-toggle <choice>'\n\nFailing tests:\n  - test_notes_prompt_fires_with_both_ages\n  - test_notes_prompt_uses_seconds_under_one_minute\n  - test_notes_prompt_uses_days_when_old\n  - test_notes_prompt_omits_last_session_clause_when_transcript_absent\n  - test_notes_prompt_fires_in_case_4_mode_active\n\nSurfaced by the migration's first real Woodpecker run (GitHub dev refresh push, pipeline 6). Because they pass natively, this is a hermeticity gap: the tests depend on lab-notebook / agent_notes state (and/or AUTONOMOUS_MODE precedence and transcript presence) that the fresh container lacks. They will redden the full-suite cron's test-agent-infra step and the nightly matrix wherever tests/ runs in a clean container.\n\nFix: make the tests control EVERY input the session-start hook branches on (agent_notes.json presence + mtime, AUTONOMOUS_MODE state, transcript presence) via tmp fixtures/env, so the intended branch fires regardless of ambient repo/container state. Verify by running in a clean checkout with no ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook.\n\nRepro (passes natively; needs a clean container to fail):\n  python -m pytest tests/test_session_start_agent_notes.py -o addopts=\"\" -q"  # 8c0d
    fields: {}  # 8c0d
