- op: discuss  # 1223
  at: '2026-07-26T03:05:22Z'  # 1223
  by: agent  # 1223
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1223
  clock: 3  # 1223
  nonce: '1223'  # 1223
  message: "Fixed in GitHub PR #6. Root cause CORRECTED: not an uncontrolled-inputs/hermeticity gap (the tests already fake HOME + notes + transcript) but a MISSING jq binary in the per-PR Woodpecker gate's pytest step. session_start_logic.sh's 'command -v jq' guard (line 91) returns early with no jq -> the notes prompt never appends -> the 5 'prompt fires' assertions fail. Sibling steps (hook-tests:149, forge-arms:173) and full-suite's test-agent-infra:103 already install jq; the main pytest step was the lone omission (surfaced by pipeline 6's whole-suite run). Fix: add 'apt-get install -y jq' to that step. Behavioral evidence: reproduced by masking jq from PATH -> exactly these 5 fail (assert 'false' == 'true'); with jq present all 9 pass. Caveats: PR #6's gate did not re-select these 5 (smart-test picked only cli.py-affected tests), so the direct in-CI observation lands on the next gate run that selects them -- the mechanism is locally proven + the fix is in dev. The item's prediction that full-suite/nightly would redden was inaccurate (full-suite already had jq; nightly runs only packages/*/tests/, not top-level tests/)."  # 1223
